CARVE-OUT — docs/GACHA-RATE-DESIGN-LOCK.md

Copyright (c) 2026 HetCreep. All rights reserved.

The MIT grant above does NOT apply to docs/GACHA-RATE-DESIGN-LOCK.md. That file
is licensed separately under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives
4.0 International (CC BY-NC-ND 4.0), same terms as the SPRITE-DESIGN-LOCK.md
carve-out above:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/

You may read it, quote it with attribution, and share it unchanged for
non-commercial purposes. You may not use it commercially, and you may not
distribute a modified version, without a separate written licence from the
copyright holder.

STANDING GRANT — Katomnoi Studio (github.com/KatomnoiStudio)

Katomnoi Studio is granted a perpetual, irrevocable, royalty-free licence to
use, reproduce, modify, and create derivative works from
docs/GACHA-RATE-DESIGN-LOCK.md, and to apply it in the Studio's own products
and services, including commercially. This grant does NOT include the right
to sublicense that file, or to distribute it or substantial portions of it to
third parties — the Studio may freely ship whatever it BUILDS from the
document (the migration, the config, the game itself); the document itself
remains the copyright holder's to license.

SCOPE AND LIMITS OF THIS CARVE-OUT — read before relying on it

  1. It applies from the commit that introduces it onward, same as the
     SPRITE-DESIGN-LOCK.md carve-out.

  2. "LegendofSoulTH" in the MIT notice above is a project name, not a legal
     person — unsettled, same open point as the sprite carve-out above.

  3. This file is unusually fact-heavy even for a design lock: real drop rates,
     pity thresholds, and prices pulled from six live games (with source URLs
     in the file itself), Thai and comparator-country minimum/average wage
     figures, and formulas derived mechanically from those inputs. None of
     that is copyrightable — facts and formulas are not protected subject
     matter in most jurisdictions, regardless of how much work went into
     finding them. What this carve-out protects is the specific SELECTION of
     which exemplars to compare, the ARRANGEMENT of the derivation (band
     splits, pity formulas, the shard-freeze decision, the final ratified
     numbers for this project), and the EXPRESSION — not the underlying facts,
     and not the numbers a reader could independently derive from the same
     public sources.

  4. The document's core price derivation (§11.8, `c`) is anchored to
     Thailand's own minimum and average wage data specifically — burden
     measured against a Thai day's wage, not a converted foreign price. The
     work of producing this document was commissioned and ratified inside
     Thailand, for a Thai-market game, at Thai labour cost. That anchoring is
     part of why this is licensed as a standalone Thai-market economic
     artefact rather than folded into the repository's general MIT grant or
     published as a general engineering standard the way SPRITE-DESIGN-LOCK.md
     was — it is not written to generalise past this project's own market.

  5. This carve-out was drafted by an AI assistant at the owner's direction and
     has NOT been reviewed by a lawyer. It is not legal advice. If anything of
     value depends on it — in particular whether the "selection and
     arrangement" of publicly-sourced game economy data clears the originality
     bar in the relevant jurisdiction — have a lawyer settle that before
     relying on this carve-out.
